  "meta": {
    "title": "Why There's No Bridge Between Europe and Africa 🌉🇪🇸🇲🇦",
    "description": "At the Strait of Gibraltar, Europe 🇪🇸 and Africa 🇲🇦 are only about 14.2 km apart. So why no bridge? 🌉 The sea there is 300 to 900 m deep, and two strong currents pass through it: lighter Atlantic water flows in on top, while heavy, salty Mediterranean water flows out underneath 🌊 Spain and Morocco have studied an undersea rail tunnel since the 1980s, but after four decades of talks it still hasn't been built 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "Only 14 km between Europe and Africa… and still no bridge 🤯🌉",
      "Would you rather cross by bridge or tunnel? 👇",
      "Which strait should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
